Mindmap Markdown — Licensing
============================

This repository contains two kinds of material, licensed differently.


1. SPECIFICATION TEXT AND DOCUMENTATION
---------------------------------------

Licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License
(CC-BY-4.0). See LICENSE-CC-BY-4.0 for the full text, or visit:

    https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

This covers:

    spec.md
    docs/**
    rfcs/**
    README.md, GOVERNANCE.md, CONTRIBUTING.md, CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md,
    SECURITY.md, CLAUDE.md, and other prose documents

You are free to share and adapt this material, including for commercial
purposes, provided you give appropriate credit. Translations and derivative
specifications are explicitly welcome.


2. SOURCE CODE, TOOLING, AND TEST DATA
--------------------------------------

Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. See LICENSE-APACHE-2.0 for
the full text, or visit:

    https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0

This covers:

    tools/**
    examples/**
    scripts, workflows, and any other executable or machine-readable artifact

The Apache License grants an explicit patent license to implementers. This is
deliberate: an implementer of an open specification should not be exposed to
patent risk arising from that implementation.


WHY TWO LICENSES
----------------

Specification text and code have different reuse expectations. Standards
documents are quoted, translated, and republished, which a documentation
license accommodates and a source-code license does not. Conversely, reference
tooling needs an explicit patent grant, which Creative Commons licenses do not
provide.

Separating them is normal practice for open specifications and avoids
ambiguity for anyone implementing this specification.


CONTRIBUTIONS
-------------

Unless you state otherwise, any contribution you intentionally submit for
inclusion in this repository shall be licensed as above, with no additional
terms or conditions.

Contributions are accepted under the Developer Certificate of Origin (DCO).
See CONTRIBUTING.md.


SPDX
----

    Documentation:  CC-BY-4.0
    Code:           Apache-2.0
